Answer: You can use a higher level API, such as [puppeteer-extra](https://github.com/GoogleChrome/puppeteer/tree/master/packages/puppeteer-extra):

\begin{code}
// Install puppeteer-extra
npm i puppeteer-extra

// Get the translation result
const response = await page.evaluate(() => {
  const selector = 'p';
  const results = document.querySelector(selector).innerText;
  return results;
});

// Output the translation result
console.log(response);
\end{code}

Also you can use `'input[name="q"]'` in `evaluate` function instead of `'p'` in `evaluate` function.

Comment: You need to add the prefix `page.evaluate` to the `await page.evaluate` line.

